                                "sense_id": "7a3f0c0b-87b8-368c-a55c-af62e3b9fce6",
                                "text": "Aleuromancy and alphitomancy were almost analogous processes; cakes were made of wheat or barley flour which could not be swallowed by anyone guilty of a given misdeed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
